ions","Terms with Thai translations","Terms with Tibetan translations","Terms with Tulu translations","Terms with Turkish translations","Terms with Ukrainian translations","Terms with Urdu translations","Terms with Vietnamese translations","Terms with Waray-Waray translations","Terms with Welsh translations","Terms with Western Punjabi translations","Terms with Yiddish translations","en:Karnataka, India","en:Places in India","en:States and union territories of India"],"links":[["state","state"],["India","India#English"],["Bengaluru","Bengaluru#English"]],"glosses":["A state in southern India. Capital: Bengaluru."],"id":"3ee66185-9a28-4cec-9f52-75d081a8436b"}],"related":[{"word":"Carnatic"},{"word":"Kannada"}],"synonyms":[{"sense":"former name","word":"Mysore"}]},"karelian":{"id":"28e98eff-2e1c-4a2e-822c-84356a2c3bc7","word":"Karelian","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"language","tags":["masculine"],"word":"carélio"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"language","tags":["masculine"],"word":"kareliano"}],"pos":"name","tags":null,"senses":[{"links":[["Finnish","Finnish"],["Karelia","Karelia"],["Russia","Russia"],["Finland","Finland"]],"glosses":["A language closely related to Finnish, spoken in Karelia, Russia and Finland."],"id":"7c375b10-c841-41b3-8337-1e528dec3c79"}],"related":[{"word":"Wiktionary’s coverage of Karelian terms"}],"synonyms":[]},"karaoke":{"id":"7675e0e8-720c-499c-ab62-0a3f75f2401f","word":"karaoke","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"a form of entertainment","tags":["Brazil"],"word":"karaokê"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"a form of entertainment","tags":["Portugal"],"word":"karaoke"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"a form of entertainment","tags":["Portugal"],"word":"caraoque"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"a form of entertainment","tags":["Brazil"],"word":"caraoquê"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"The karaoke has been well received by those who frequent the oriental cabaret scene and adopt its particular social behaviors such as conversation, companionship, being seen, and showing off.","ref":"1993 March, Michael J. Wagner with John S. Brick, “Using Karaoke in the Classroom”, in Music Educators Journal, volume 79, number 7, →ISSN, →JSTOR, page 44:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[4,11]],"id":"09fb6147-797f-4682-8516-d1f37010134e"},{"text":"American Idol will always have a place in my heart. It's where I met Clay. And what could be more exciting than televised karaoke?","ref":"2006 February 24, Real Time with Bill Maher, season 7, episode 2, Bill Maher (actor):","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[122,129]],"id":"27bf6058-c4c9-4d4a-909d-c3acb321419c"},{"text":"I was always split on Henley. Then I found out that he doesn’t want people to sing his songs at karaoke. In fact, Henley actually forbids karaoke companies from rerecording songs in his catalog.","ref":"2008 December 9, Brian Raftery, Don't Stop Believin': How Karaoke Conquered the World and Changed My Life, Cambridge: Da Capo Press, →ISBN, →LCCN, →OCLC, →OL, page 1:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[96,103],[138,145]],"id":"063e519a-8e83-4826-a129-6191d6af8eec"},{"text":"A country that's enriched the world with sushi, karaoke and manga, Japan has many devotees, especially among gamers and geeks.","ref":"2021 April 25, John Malathronas, “Which languages are easiest – and most difficult – for native English speakers to learn?”, in CNN, archived from the original on 22 Mar 2022:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[48,55]],"id":"6a95c6e5-c5ec-42bd-896b-c8c79a6fecd7"}],"wikidata":["Q229345"],"senseid":["en:Q229345"],"categories":["English terms with quotations","English uncountable nouns"],"links":[["entertainment","entertainment"],["club","club"],["parties","parties"],["public","public"],["pre-recorded","pre-recorded"],["instrumental version","instrumental version"],["popular","popular"],["song","song"],["lyrics","lyrics"],["display","display"],["singer","singer"],["screen","screen"],["music","music"]],"raw_glosses":["(uncountable) A form of entertainment popular in clubs, at parties, etc, in which individual members of the public sing along to pre-recorded instrumental versions of popular songs, the lyrics of which are displayed for the singer on a screen in time with the music."],"glosses":["A form of entertainment popular in clubs, at parties, etc, in which individual members of the public sing along to pre-recorded instrumental versions of popular songs, the lyrics of which are displayed for the singer on a screen in time with the music."],"tags":["uncountable"],"id":"644ea51a-6278-48a9-b1e3-6c593d0f25dc"},{"categories":["English countable nouns"],"raw_glosses":["(countable) A karaoke session."],"glosses":["A karaoke session."],"tags":["countable"],"id":"602fb470-9e1b-49dc-9ed7-e38f08713dd9"},{"categories":["English countable nouns"],"synonyms":[{"word":"noraebang","tags":["especially"],"raw_tags":["in the Korean context"]}],"raw_glosses":["(countable) A karaoke parlour."],"glosses":["A karaoke parlour."],"tags":["countable"],"id":"fc1f17d4-ac0a-48be-8ce4-181844fc1d92"},{"topics":["exercise","hobbies","lifestyle","sports"],"categories":["en:Exercise"],"links":[["exercise","exercise"],["lower body","lower body"],["core","core"]],"raw_glosses":["(exercise) An exercise in which the feet are alternately placed in front of each other while walking sideways to stretch various parts of the lower body and core."],"glosses":["An exercise in which the feet are alternately placed in front of each other while walking sideways to stretch various parts of the lower body and core."],"tags":["countable","uncountable"],"id":"d9b1f9fe-bcb5-4bcf-9ddb-e1153ba6cfff"}],"related":[{"word":"karate"},{"word":"a cappella"},{"word":"amateur hour"},{"word":"amateur night"},{"word":"bathroom singer"},{"word":"KTV"},{"word":"open mic"}],"synonyms":[]},"karma":{"id":"96feb419-551f-4e46-bd71-bf0cc47c40c3","word":"karma","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"the total effect of a person’s actions and conduct during the successive phases of his existence","tags":["masculine"],"word":"carma"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"the total effect of a person’s actions and conduct during the successive phases of his existence","tags":["masculine"],"word":"karma"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"destiny, fate","tags":["masculine"],"word":"carma"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"destiny, fate","tags":["masculine"],"word":"karma"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"distinctive feeling, aura or atmosphere","tags":["masculine"],"word":"clima"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"‘We are all part of a circle of karma. We will be rewarded for the good deeds of our forefathers, and pay the price for their sins.’","ref":"2023, Santanu Bhattacharya, One Small Voice, Fig Tree, pages 59-60:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[32,37]],"id":"a8e2b55d-d2f2-44bb-b01d-f32869aacc94"}],"topics":["Buddhism","lifestyle","religion"],"categories":["English terms with quotations","en:Buddhism","en:Hinduism","en:Jainism","en:Sikhism"],"links":[["Hinduism","Hinduism"],["Buddhism","Buddhism"],["Sikhism","Sikhism"],["Jainism","Jainism"],["action","action"],["determine","determine"],["incarnation","incarnation"],["samsara","samsara"],["death","death"],["rebirth","rebirth"]],"raw_glosses":["(Hinduism, Buddhism, Sikhism, Jainism) The sum total of a person's actions, which determine the person's next incarnation in samsara, the cycle of death and rebirth."],"glosses":["The sum total of a person's actions, which determine the person's next incarnation in samsara, the cycle of death and rebirth."],"tags":["Hinduism","Jainism","Sikhism","countable","uncountable"],"id":"d406c9c5-c06d-4076-b910-bfde8fe6f6dd"},{"links":[["reap what one sows","reap what one sows"]],"glosses":["A force or law of nature which causes one to reap what one sows; destiny; fate."],"tags":["countable","uncountable"],"id":"d0d443eb-1a10-459d-a42d-f260781ceff5"},{"examples":[{"text":"That means everything from lighting to the vibes, the karma of the room.","ref":"2001, Inside the Hits, page 307:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[54,59]],"id":"42453bb4-26d6-4942-93a4-32adca12a66c"},{"text":"How many times when you have been in a bar have you felt that a confrontation was building up, even without extensive verbal exchanges? Sometimes you can feel the karma or energy of a place change, and you should not ignore that","ref":"2006, Chase Sargent, From Buddy to Boss, page 219:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[163,168]],"id":"89bd4197-0fa2-427d-b530-576138505701"},{"text":"On the way to Lancaster, which was about an hour and a half from Philly, John felt the karma.","ref":"2010, R.L. Roach, Irish Lie, page 135:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[87,92]],"id":"39528d56-0003-488f-b108-7b25f504f537"}],"categories":["English terms with quotations","English terms with uncommon senses","Quotation templates to be cleaned"],"links":[["distinctive","distinctive"],["feeling","feeling"],["aura","aura"],["atmosphere","atmosphere"]],"raw_glosses":["(uncommon) A distinctive feeling, aura, or atmosphere."],"glosses":["A distinctive feeling, aura, or atmosphere."],"tags":["countable","uncommon","uncountable"],"id":"975eb619-7538-4ef4-9d93-506669036571"},{"categories":["en:Internet"],"links":[["Internet","Internet"],["score","score"],["user","user"],["post","post"],["discussion","discussion"],["forums","forum"],["popularity","popularity"],["value","value"]],"raw_glosses":["(Internet) A score assigned to a user or post on some discussion forums, indicating popularity or perceived value."],"glosses":["A score assigned to a user or post on some discussion forums, indicating popularity or perceived value."],"tags":["Internet","countable","uncountable"],"id":"b981aae1-4d8a-4be3-a272-bab8f78f9e77"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[]},"karate":{"id":"d70e349a-2776-4a1a-944e-09b636208dc3","word":"karate","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"martial art","tags":["masculine"],"word":"caratê"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"martial art","tags":["masculine"],"word":"karaté"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"martial art","tags":["masculine"],"word":"caraté"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"Prior to the coronavirus pandemic, Wall taught karate at a local nursing home.","ref":"2020 June 10, Ashley Vaughan, “This teenage martial artist creates videos to help superhero seniors stay active while in quarantine”, in CNN:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[47,53]],"id":"71a72044-4500-4f2c-9d0e-fd51c6aa4ad8"}],"links":[["martial art","martial art"],["punch","punch"],["kick","kick"],["arm bar","arm bar"]],"categories":["English terms with quotations"],"glosses":["An Okinawan martial art involving primarily punching and kicking, but additionally, advanced throws, arm bars, grappling and all means of fighting."],"tags":["uncountable"],"id":"0cf7d24f-4a04-4c42-a005-97065aca3537"}],"related":[{"word":"karateka"}],"synonyms":[]},"karbala":{"id":"1eb6fa92-7515-4cc8-bf08-0451ce192414","word":"Karbala","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"Translations","word":"Carbala"}],"pos":"name","tags":null,"senses":[{"wikidata":["Q199909"],"senseid":["en:Q199909"],"categories":["English entries with incorrect language header","English lemmas","English proper nouns","English terms borrowed from Arabic","English terms derived from Arabic","English uncountable nouns","Entries with translation boxes","Pages with 1 entry","Pages with entries","Terms with Arabic translations","Terms with Chinese translations","Terms with Dutch translations","Terms with French translations","Terms with German translations","Terms with Italian translations","Terms with Ottoman Turkish translations","Terms with Persian translations","Terms with Portuguese translations","Terms with Russian translations","Terms with Spanish translations","Terms with Turkish translations","Terms with Urdu translations","Translation table header lacks gloss","en:Cities in Iraq","en:Islam","en:Places in Iraq"],"links":[["city","city"],["Iraq","Iraq#English"],["site","site"],["murder","murder"],["major","major"],["pilgrimage","pilgrimage"],["destination","destination"],["Shiite","Shiite"],["Muslim","Muslim"]],"glosses":["A city in central Iraq, site of the murder of Husayn ibn Ali and major pilgrimage destination for Shiite Muslims."],"id":"51201639-d69b-4ae3-a295-230da8691598"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[]},"karst":{"id":"66e36914-31e1-4190-bb96-2a8a829425d8","word":"karst","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"type of land formation","tags":["masculine"],"word":"carso"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"type of land formation","tags":["masculine"],"word":"carste"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"In the time available to us on our geomorphological tour we were not able to see the higher and younger karsts of Kweichow and Yunnan and Kunming.","ref":"1978, M. M. Sweeting, “The Karst of Kweilin, Southern China”, in The Geographical Journal, volume 144, number 2, page 200:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[104,110]],"id":"da4f57f1-993d-4677-86e1-e1607ff3132b"},{"text":"The shells are just 0.04 inch (one millimeter) long and were found on a karst formation where conditions are damp, but the snails that inhabit them have yet to be observed.","ref":"2009 May 29, “Katherine Harmon”, in Top 10 New Species Discovered in 2008^([ScientificAmerican.com]):","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[72,77]],"id":"2901f20a-c647-4056-85af-576c7612a40b"}],"topics":["geography","geology","natural-sciences"],"categories":["English countable nouns","English entries with incorrect language header","English lemmas","English nouns","English terms borrowed from German","English terms derived from German","English terms derived from Italo-Dalmatian languages","English terms derived from Proto-Indo-European","English terms derived from Proto-Slavic","English terms derived from Slovene","English terms with homophones","English terms with quotations","Entries with translation boxes","Pages with 6 entries","Pages with entries","Rhymes:English/ɑː(ɹ)st","Rhymes:English/ɑː(ɹ)st/1 syllable","Terms with Aragonese translations","Terms with Armenian translations","Terms with Azerbaijani translations","Terms with Belarusian translations","Terms with Bulgarian translations","Terms with Cantonese translations","Terms with Catalan translations","Terms with Czech translations","Terms with Dutch translations","Terms with Esperanto translations","Terms with Finnish translations","Terms with French translations","Terms with German translations","Terms with Hungarian translations","Terms with Icelandic translations","Terms with Irish translations","Terms with Italian translations","Terms with Japanese translations","Terms with Macedonian translations","Terms with Mandarin translations","Terms with Norwegian translations","Terms with Polish translations","Terms with Portuguese translations","Terms with Russian translations","Terms with Serbo-Croatian translations","Terms with Slovene translations","Terms with Spanish translations","Terms with Tagalog translations","Terms with Vietnamese translations","Terms with Welsh translations","en:Geology"],"links":[["geology","geology"],["land","land"],["formation","formation"],["cave","cave"],["limestone","limestone"],["underground","underground"],["drainage","drainage"]],"raw_glosses":["(geology) A type of land formation, usually with many caves formed through the dissolving of limestone by underground drainage."],"glosses":["A type of land formation, usually with many caves formed through the dissolving of limestone by underground drainage."],"wikipedia":["Karst Plateau (Italy-Slovenia)"],"id":"9914a28d-f7d7-4d1d-b102-0f89c4c75d74"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[]},"karen":{"id":"6e4f6748-bddb-453a-9903-e5c93900fa37","word":"Karen","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"female given name","tags":["feminine"],"word":"Karen"}],"pos":"name","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"Left you a lover in that far land, / O Karen sad, that you pine so long! / Would I could unravel and understand / That sorrowful, sweet Norwegian song!","ref":"1878 Celia Thaxter, Drift-Weed, Houghton, Osgood,1878, page 28 (\"Karen\")","id":"7891db2d-e731-435b-8280-08381c693e07"},{"text":"I was not called Karen after Hans Andersen's dancing girl, but after a Danish friend of my mother's who married an Englishman and was my godmother. So much for our family affairs.","ref":"1918 Cecily Ullman Sidgwick, Karen, W.Collins, 1918, page 12","id":"5672451d-d518-4669-8afd-75248c7d4b43"},{"text":"“There’s a sense of betrayal,” said the former Hamtramck mayor Karen Majewski, who is Polish American.","ref":"2023 June 17, Tom Perkins, “‘A sense of betrayal’: liberal dismay as Muslim-led US city bans Pride flags”, in The Guardian, archived from the original on 10 Aug 2023:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[63,68]],"id":"6fede437-4639-4d11-a42a-d9048c985c93"}],"categories":["English female given names","English female given names from Ancient Greek","English given names","English terms with quotations"],"links":[["given name","given name"]],"glosses":["A female given name from Ancient Greek."],"id":"4e87735c-4157-45e7-b721-16a6150e6b64"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[]},"kare":{"id":"05c39f76-d70d-45b4-a49c-6e12a538a3d0","word":"Kare","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"village in Žitorađa, Toplica, Serbia","word":"Kare"}],"pos":"name","tags":null,"senses":[{"categories":["en:Places in Serbia","en:Villages in Serbia"],"links":[["village","village"],["Žitorađa","Žitorađa#English"],["Toplica","Toplica#English"],["Serbia","Serbia#English"]],"glosses":["A village in Žitorađa, Toplica okrug, Serbia."],"id":"a30c848c-5a62-4c8e-9c03-9e0bea419a45"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[]},"karmic":{"id":"c83d0de1-c8ec-4b0c-91aa-b7d67d51ebfb","word":"karmic","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"of or pertaining to karma","word":"cármico"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"of or pertaining to karma","word":"kármico"}],"pos":"adj","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"Ken Kesey was one who supported abortion only to save the life of the mother, arguing that society needed to care about everyone, including “the un-dead old [and]^([sic]) the un-born young.” As he put it, “Abortions are a terrible karmic bummer.”","ref":"1991, Timothy Miller, quoting Ken Kesey, The hippies and American values, University of Tennessee Press, →ISBN, page 65:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[231,237]],"id":"f297d27a-392d-42da-ad38-6b86da7d3402"},{"text":"Raymond Gunt is not a nice person. He might just be, as more than one character in Douglas Coupland’s 14th novel remarks, the Worst. Person. Ever. He’s far-fetchedly horrible. A grotesque. A supernova of bad karmic energy.","ref":"2013 September 29, “Book review: Worst. Person. Ever. By Douglas Coupland”, in The Independent, London: Independent News & Media, →ISSN, →OCLC, archived from the original on 23 Aug 2014:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[208,214]],"id":"84372d08-e796-4611-bd0f-fb3b29881090"}],"links":[["karma","karma"]],"categories":["English adjectives","English entries with incorrect language header","English lemmas","English terms suffixed with -ic","English terms with quotations","English uncomparable adjectives","Entries with translation boxes","Pages with 1 entry","Pages with entries","Requests for review of